'''Kijimi''' was a [[Temperature|frigid]] [[mountain]]ous [[planet]] located in the [[Bryx sector]] of [[the galaxy]]'s [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]], in grid square R-8 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]]. Once famed for its marked spirituality, the planet became known as a haven for criminals and lawlessness. It was the [[homeworld]] of [[Zorii Bliss]], leader of the [[Smuggler|smuggling]] gang known as the [[Spice Runners of Kijimi]]. During their journey around the [[galaxy]] to uncover [[Jedi artifact]]s, [[Karr Nuq Sin]] and [[RZ-7]] briefly stopped at [[Kijimi City]] to [[Fuel|refuel]] the [[yacht]] ''[[Avadora]]''. While on Kijimi, Sin was questioned by the [[First Order]] as they believed he had a [[Map to Skywalker|clue]] to finding [[Jedi Master]] [[Luke Skywalker]]. In [[35 ABY]], Kijimi was [[Destruction of Kijimi|obliterated]] by the [[Xyston-class Star Destroyer|''Xyston-class'' Star Destroyer]] ''[[Derriphan]]'' of the [[Sith Eternal]]'s [[fleet]], the [[Final Order]].

==Description==
{{Quote|So this is Kijimi, huh? Looks cold and dark.|Kay Vess|<ref name="Outlaws" />}}
A terrestrial [[planet]], Kijimi had [[mountain]]ous terrain. Due to its extreme orbital distance from its star, the planet received minimal sunlight and had a [[Temperature|frigid]] climate, with thick drifts of [[Water|snow]] covering its mountains. Despite this, subterranean volcanic activity ensured enough liquid water existed on the surface to support organic life. The [[atmosphere]] of Kijimi was breathable to a number of inhabitants, including [[human]]s,<ref name="Force Collector" /> [[Boosodian]]s, and [[Anzellan]]s. The planet was adjacent to a [[Kijimi Nebula|nebula]].<ref name="Outlaws" />

Kijimi had no central government<ref name="Outlaws" /> and was effectively an anarchy with some stability. The self interests of members of the population kept the planet society from collapsing.<ref name="TROSVD" /> The arrival of the [[First Order]], however, created a new governing body that made its presence known via a [[Occupation of Kijimi|brutal occupation]], a clear difference from the freedom-defined era that Kijimi had known before the occupation.<ref name="KashyyykEncyc">{{EncyclopediaCite|Kashyyyk and Other Planets in the Mid Rim}}</ref>

==History==
===Early history===
A thousand years ago, a [[Religion|religious]] group known as [[Dai Bendu]] constructed a [[Dai Bendu Monastery|monastery]] on the planet in the center of what became [[Kijimi City]]. During the cold nights, Bendu monks held a [[Dai Bendu lantern ceremony|ceremony]] of lighting the [[lantern]]s to express gratitude. The existence of the temple prompted the [[Brotherhood of the Beatific Countenance]] to make a pilgrimage to Kijimi, inhabiting the [[Thieves' Quarter|Quarter of the Beatific]]. Over the centuries, the city was periodically raided and the monks disappeared.<ref name="TROSVD" />

===High Republic Era===
During the [[High Republic Era]], a [[Melitto]] [[Melitto hive|hive]] known as the [[Ashiga Clan]] established itself on Kijimi, becoming a prominent force in the planet's underworld.<ref name="Outlaws" />

===Imperial Era===
{{Quote|We don't need the Outer Rim. Our place is here!|Krisk Ashiga, to Queen Ashiga|<ref name="Outlaws" />}}
[[File:KijimiNebulaTrailblazer-Outlaws.jpg|thumb|right|250px|With control of the planet at stake, the Trailblazer ship, piloted by [[Kay Vess]], approaches Kijimi.]]
During the [[Imperial Era]], the [[queen]] of the Ashiga Clan, [[Ashiga]], was admired for resisting the [[Galactic Empire]] on Kijimi. However, during the [[Galactic Civil War]], she relented and provided the Empire access to the planet for its [[rhydonium]] mines in exchange for weapons contracts. Her decision caused division within the ranks of the Ashiga Clan and several members, including her own daughter [[Krisk Ashiga]], began to formulate plans to overthrow her.<ref name="Outlaws" /> At that time, the clan's control over Kijimi was also weakening.<ref name="Overview">{{Twitter|username=StarWarsOutlaws|url=status/1824838649650749743|name=''[[Star Wars Outlaws]]''|date=2024-08-17|quote=Order and hierarchy are the tenets of the Ashiga Clan - will you stay in their good books or be just another sacrifice for the cause?|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/Jb6Up}}</ref> [[Crimson Dawn]], a crime syndicate that was interested in taking control of Kijimi, was vying for power on the planet with the Ashiga Clan, going so far as to steal a relic important to them, the Bann Pu'dira. Krisk made an alliance with the Crimson Dawn to dethrone her mother. Lady [[Qi'ra]] and Crimson Dawn helped Krisk as the leadership change could favor Crimson Dawn.<ref name="Outlaws" />

===New Republic Era===
{{Quote|Although&hellip;I did hear my dad talking yesterday, and he mentioned a place called Kijimi. If it's not too out of the way, maybe you can stop there for fuel and check it out for me.|Maize Raynshi, to Karr Nuq Sin|<ref name="Force Collector" />}}
[[File:KijimiCity-DB.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Kijimi City continued to be ruled by the anarchy of criminal self-interests.]]
With the collapse of the Galactic Empire, lawlessness ran rampant in parts of the galaxy during the [[New Republic Era|era]] of the [[New Republic]], which was too weak to pacify deeply criminalized worlds, and its failure lead to widespread apathy. The Empire's fall also lead to a shake up in the [[spice]] trade based on [[Kessel]]. Competition for the spice trade increased. The pirates of Kjiimi struck a deal with the mine owners that allowed for an exclusive route in an expanded Kessel Run.<ref name="TROSVD" />

Eventually, [[Maize Raynshi]], the daughter of the [[First Order officer]] [[Vroc Raynshi]], overheard her [[Parent|father]] mention Kijimi, and asked her friend [[Karr Nuq Sin]] to check out the planet on his search for [[Jedi artifact]]s. Nuq Sin and his [[droid]], [[RZ-7]], landed the [[yacht]] ''[[Avadora]]'' at the [[Kijimi Spaceport|spaceport]] in [[Kijimi City]] to [[Fuel|refuel]], and wandered the streets of the [[city]] for some [[time]]. When Nuq Sin returned to the ''Avadora'', which Nuq Sin had stolen from Vroc Raynshi with the help of Maize, it was surrounded by [[First Order]] [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtroopers]]. An [[officer]] of the First Order then questioned Nuq Sin, believing he possessed a [[Map to Skywalker|map]] that led to the lost [[Jedi Master]] [[Luke Skywalker]]. Once the First Order released Nuq Sin, he left Kijimi, returning to his [[homeworld]] of [[Merokia]].<ref name="Force Collector" />

===First Order occupation===
{{Quote|Here's your ship. We didn't steal it, we just borrowed it from Maize. I'm sorry, but I'm done with it now, anyway. Just take us home already.''"<br />"''Home? You're not going anywhere. First, you're going to answer some questions.|Karr Nuq Sin and a First Order officer|<ref name="Force Collector" />}}
[[File:KijimiGarrison-TROSVD.jpg|thumb|right|250px|The First Order seized Kijimi and imposed martial law on the criminalized world.]]
The First Order had a brutal [[Occupation of Kijimi|occupation]] on the planet. Martial law was imposed and all major hyperspace routes were blockaded. Most of the planet's children were taken early in the occupation. First Order teams regularly patrolled the city, searching for illegal or rebel activity or children to kidnap and conscript into stormtroopers.<ref name="Episode IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

The scoundrel [[Zorii Bliss]] led the [[Spice Runners of Kijimi]] [[Smuggler|smuggling]] gang during the [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] between the First Order and the [[Resistance]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars NE" /> Residing in the [[Thieves' Quarter]],<ref name="TROSVD" /> Bliss and the Spice Runners stayed neutral in the ongoing war until they were eventually wiped out by the occupation forces. Only Zorii and the [[Anzellan]] [[droidsmith]] [[Babu Frik]] survived gang's destruction.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars NE" />

===Destruction of Kijimi===
{{Quote|Captain, Kijimi is in range.''"<br />"''Fire.|Milon Lenwith and Chesille Sabrond|<ref name="Episode IX" />}}
[[File:KijimiGoBoom-TROS.png|thumb|left|250px|Kijimi is destroyed by the ''Derriphan''.]]
The First Order issued [[Protocol 13]] and removed all stormtroopers from the planet.<ref name="TROSVD" /> Kijimi was then [[Destruction of Kijimi|destroyed]] by the [[Sith Eternal]] with the [[Xyston-class Star Destroyer|''Xyston''-class Star Destroyer]] ''[[Derriphan]]'' of the [[Final Order]] [[fleet]].<ref name="Episode IX" />

Most inhabitants were killed as the planet was destroyed, but Zorii Bliss and Babu Frik managed to survive by boarding a [[Comeuppance|ship]] and escaping seconds before destruction.<ref name="TROS Expanded">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Expanded Edition]]''</ref>

==Inhabitants==
{{Quote|Everyone else is dressed for it.|Karr Nuq Sin, on Kijimi's climate|<ref name="Force Collector" />}}
[[File:ZoriiKijimiLeibovitz.jpg|thumb|right|300px|Zorii Bliss, a human native of Kijimi]]
Kijimi had a number of inhabitants,<ref name="Force Collector" /> including the [[human]] Zorii Bliss, who was native to the planet.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars NE" /> The residents of Kijimi wore thick [[Hair|furs]] and animal hides to combat the cold climate. While on Kijimi, Karr Nuq Sin was unnerved by the disreputable appearance of many of its residents.<ref name="Force Collector" />

The [[Anzellan]] [[droidsmith]] [[Babu Frik]] also lived on the planet, working among the Spice Runners of Kijimi.<ref name="TROSVD" /> Many [[Melitto]] were present on Kijimi as part of the Ashiga Clan,<ref name="Outlaws" /> whose control over Kijimi eventually weakened.<ref name="Overview" />

==Locations==
Kijimi City, home to a [[spaceport]], was located on the peak of [[Mount Izukika]], almost hidden between the mountains and the snow. The ancient architecture of the city reminded Karr Nuq Sin of old monasteries.<ref name="Force Collector" /> The Thieves' Quarter was a region of Kijimi where the scoundrel Zorii Bliss resided.<ref name="TROSVD" />

==Behind the scenes==
Kijimi was created for the [[2019]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']].<ref name="Episode IX" /> It first appeared in the novel ''[[Force Collector]]'', written by [[Kevin Shinick]] and published in 2019.<ref name="Force Collector" />

Kijimi shares its name with a synthesizer from Tokyo's Black Corporation. Director [[J.J. Abrams]] is a known customer of the company and can be seen posing with a Kijimi synthesizer in an Instagram post by the company.<ref name="Synth">{{WebCite|url=https://cdm.link/2019/12/kijimi-star-wars-planet|text=Kijimi, key planet in new Star Wars flick, is named after the synthesizer|author=kirn, Peter|date=2019-12-21|archivedate=20200514142755}}</ref>

